              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_7_table_7.jpg",
              "content": "<table><tr><td colspan=\"4\">Explanation with Algebra and Visualisation Examples</td></tr><tr><td>Numbers divisible by 7 will have 7 as a factor.</td><td colspan=\"2\">7j</td><td><eq>14 = 7 \\times 2 (j = 2).</eq> <eq>42 = 7 \\times 6 (j = 6).</eq> <eq>98 = 7 \\times 14 (j = 14).</eq></td></tr><tr><td>This contains a total of mj rows. So this is also a multiple of 7.</td><td>(7j)×m</td><td><img src=\"images/page_7_table_image_7_1.jpg\"/> m times <img src=\"images/page_7_table_image_7_2.jpg\"/></td><td>Some multiples of 14: <eq>2 8 = ( 7 \\times 2 ) \\times 2 .</eq> <eq>7 0 = ( 7 \\times 2 ) \\times 5 .</eq> <eq>1 5 4 = ( 7 \\times 2 ) \\times 1 1</eq></td></tr></table>"
